---
// Shared answer key for the evidence rubric used by every question-based
// free tool. Each answer is a level of evidence, not a level of agreement:
// "choose the level you could show evidence for". Scores map 1-5 to
// 0/25/50/75/100%, the same rubric the InstitutionalOS Diagnostic verifies.
---
<details class="rubric-key" open>
  <summary>How to answer: choose the level you could <em>show evidence for</em></summary>
  <dl>
    <div><dt>1 · Not in place</dt><dd>We don't do this.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>2 · Talked about</dt><dd>Discussed or planned, but not started.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>3 · Informal</dt><dd>It happens, but isn't written down or consistent.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>4 · Documented</dt><dd>Written down and in regular use; you could show it.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>5 · Verified</dt><dd>Routine and reviewed; it would hold up if a funder or board checked.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p>If you're between two levels, pick the lower one. An honest score is more useful than a flattering one.</p>
</details>
